<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n14139" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπο-τρώγω</span></b> , aor. 2
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπέτρᾰγον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ph.
					1.224
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				6.864
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.L.
				9.27
			</span></i>:— <i>bite</i> or <i>nibble off,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πτόρθους</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Eup.
					14
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ ἱππομανὲς ἀ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>HA</u>
					605a4
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γλῶτταν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ph.
				</span></i>
			 l.c., cf. <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
			</span></i> l.c.: metaph., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μισθοὺς ἀ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Ra.</u>
					367
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Men.
				303
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. τὸ ἀπορηθέν</span> 'gulp
			down', 'bolt' the difficulty, i.e. pass it by without trying to get
			at the heart of the matter, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Metaph.</u>
				1001a2
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> c. gen.,
				<i>nibble at,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πόης</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Babr.
					46.6
				</span></i>
			: metaph., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τᾶς αὔλακος οὐκ
				ἀποτρώγεις,</span> i.e. you don't <i>gobble</i> your
			swathe, <i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				10
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>6.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπό-τρωκτος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, <i>bitten off</i>: metaph., <i>with
				the end cut off by apocope,</i> e.g. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄλφι</span> for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄλφιτον,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i> and <i><span class="en">
				Suid.
			</span></i>
			
				s.v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄλφι.</span>
			</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
